1
00:00:06,780 --> 00:00:11,060
A tiling app takes the side of a square tile, X centimetres.

2
00:00:11,110 --> 00:00:15,380
It squares it, then adds 4 square centimetres for the grout.

3
00:00:15,430 --> 00:00:17,160
The output is 85.

4
00:00:17,210 --> 00:00:18,470
What was the input?

5
00:00:18,520 --> 00:00:20,190
Give the positive answer.

6
00:00:20,240 --> 00:00:23,790
Pause the video and work it out.

7
00:00:23,840 --> 00:00:25,140
Work backwards.

8
00:00:25,190 --> 00:00:26,660
85 minus 4 is 81.

9
00:00:26,710 --> 00:00:29,090
The square root of 81 is 9.

10
00:00:29,140 --> 00:00:31,350
So the input was 9.

11
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:34,170
Remember: X, times 3, add 1, gives Y.

12
00:00:34,220 --> 00:00:36,470
So Y equals 3 X plus 1.

13
00:00:36,520 --> 00:00:39,210
A function machine can include powers.

14
00:00:39,260 --> 00:00:43,370
X, square, add 4, gives Y equals X squared plus 4.

15
00:00:43,420 --> 00:00:44,070
Your turn.

16
00:00:44,120 --> 00:00:46,030
Find Y when X is negative 3.

17
00:00:46,080 --> 00:00:49,320
Pause the video and try it.

18
00:00:49,370 --> 00:00:51,420
Negative 3 squared is 9.

19
00:00:51,470 --> 00:00:52,720
9 plus 4 is 13.

20
00:00:52,770 --> 00:00:57,720
So X equals 3 and X equals negative 3 both give 13.

21
00:00:57,770 --> 00:00:58,750
Order matters.

22
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:02,900
Square, then times 2, gives Y equals 2 X squared.

23
00:01:02,950 --> 00:01:03,620
Your turn.

24
00:01:03,670 --> 00:01:09,700
What about times 2, then square: is it Y equals 4 X squared, or Y equals 2 X squared?

25
00:01:09,750 --> 00:01:13,030
Pause the video and choose.

26
00:01:13,080 --> 00:01:16,010
Times 2 then square is 2 X, all squared.

27
00:01:16,060 --> 00:01:17,500
That is 4 X squared.

28
00:01:17,550 --> 00:01:19,840
Brackets keep the order.

29
00:01:19,890 --> 00:01:21,160
Here is the method.

30
00:01:21,210 --> 00:01:25,870
Step 1: follow the steps in order to make a table of values.

31
00:01:25,920 --> 00:01:30,760
Step 2: write the equation, using brackets to keep the order.

32
00:01:30,810 --> 00:01:34,670
Step 3: draw a mapping diagram if you need one.

33
00:01:34,720 --> 00:01:39,850
Step 4: to find an input, use inverse operations in reverse order.

34
00:01:39,900 --> 00:01:44,650
X, add 1, then square, gives Y equals X plus 1, all squared.

35
00:01:44,700 --> 00:01:46,860
Y equals X cubed minus 5.

36
00:01:46,910 --> 00:01:48,350
The output is 59.

37
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:49,240
Add 5: 64.

38
00:01:49,290 --> 00:01:51,990
The cube root of 64 is 4.

39
00:01:52,040 --> 00:01:56,380
Halve X, then square, gives Y equals X squared over 4.

40
00:01:56,430 --> 00:01:59,740
Jay writes X, add 3, then square, as an equation.

41
00:01:59,790 --> 00:02:01,660
Which line is wrong?

42
00:02:01,710 --> 00:02:02,800
Line 1 is wrong.

43
00:02:02,850 --> 00:02:06,710
The square must apply to the whole of X plus 3.

44
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:09,500
Y equals X plus 3, all squared.

45
00:02:09,550 --> 00:02:12,470
A spreadsheet formula is a function machine.

46
00:02:12,520 --> 00:02:18,220
Type a value in one cell, and the formula turns it into an output in another.

47
00:02:18,270 --> 00:02:19,490
One last question.

48
00:02:19,540 --> 00:02:20,690
Y equals X cubed.

49
00:02:20,740 --> 00:02:22,660
Find Y when X is negative 2.

50
00:02:22,710 --> 00:02:25,960
Pause the video and answer.

51
00:02:26,010 --> 00:02:31,300
Negative 2 times negative 2 times negative 2 is negative 8.

52
00:02:31,350 --> 00:02:34,500
To remember: follow the steps in order.

53
00:02:34,550 --> 00:02:38,200
Use brackets to show the order in an equation.

54
00:02:38,250 --> 00:02:42,810
Work backwards with inverse operations, in reverse order.

55
00:02:42,860 --> 00:02:46,780
With squares, two inputs can give the same output.

56
00:02:46,830 --> 00:02:51,950
Great work! Now practise lesson 9.3 on Camday.
